description:
**This job is with ESW, an inclusive employer and a member of myGwork – the largest global platform for the LGBTQ\+ business community. Please do not contact the recruiter directly.**
 e are looking for an experienced, capable Senior Principal Architect who has led architecture initiatives in or around e\-commerce or retail. They will be strategically focussed with excellent communication and stakeholder management skills; ideally formally trained in either TOGAF or Zachman frameworks. Coming from an advanced technology and software development background the Principal Architect will work with the business, engineering, product and the wider architecture team to assure ESW strategy and industry best practice is at the heart of our design thinking, and the quality of what we deliver aligns to our values. The right candidate will have a 5\+ years of experience as a Senior Enterprise, Solution Architect, or Head of Architecture working in and around key technology areas like event\-driven architecture, micro\-services, domain\-driven design and data\-driven architectures; ideally across multiple industries including Retail. Having worked with public cloud (ideally Azure) around concepts like Containers, DevSecOps, PaaS and SaaS whilst working on specifics like API management, caching/scaling in high performance environments and container driven designs with a technology like Kubernetes. We have a mixed approach to delivery pulling on our agile start\-up roots whilst balancing planning needs of the business and product to provide guidance to business, product and commercial strategy. The role will ensure that architecture processes are adhered too and work closely aligned to the existing ESW delivery processes, being involved in relevant retros to continually improve these. Reporting to the VP Architecture the role will assist in making key architecture decisions that will influence the company direction and act as role model and mentor to our partners in engineering and product. The right leader will positively influence stakeholders by demonstrating professionalism, enthusiasm, strong communication and creating collaborative environments for architecture to thrive. While frequent travel is not expected, there will be required visits to our sites in the US, Europe and Worldwide; mainly focussed in Madrid, Dublin and New York. Key Responsibilities Working closely with peers in product and the business to help define roadmaps that align business strategy to technology strategy whilst balancing client needs to timelines Creating high level designs that clearly articulate strategy and technology steer. Focussing on business requirements/capabilities, data architecture, standards, impact assessments across domains, business cases, high level implementation plans and NFRs Collaborating with engineering, product and business peers to ensure that HLDs are understood, helping shape significant solution designs whilst identifying key architecture decisions and calling out technical and architectural debt Working in an agile environment, applying “Just Enough Design”, “Adaptability” and “Assurance over Governance” Being able to become expert in one or more domains but always aware and working to align across domains to an enterprise view Ensure the right guardrails (principles, policies, standards and NFRs) are continually updated, understood and implemented across ESW. Be a positive mentor to the wider technology and product teams Create and maintain the conceptual data models, as\-is and to\-be architectures for domains and/or strategic initiatives Desired Skills TOGAF or Zachman Certified Kafka (ideally Confluent) for event\-driven architecture and event\-streaming Architectural experience of native and non\-native cloud services for either Azure or AWS including: Kubernetes, CosmosDB Understanding and able to present differences between conceptual, logical and physical architectures to a range of stakeholders from Engineering Managers to Execs Intellectual curiosity, learning agility, and enthusiasm for tackling tough problems Outstanding communication skills required \- primarily the ability to communicate ideas Deep Problem solving – the ability to analyse a business or technical problem and select the most appropriate solutions Understanding of risk in designs and mitigation strategies Experience of retail industry would be a significant advantage Experience managing monolith/legacy migration programs a huge plus! About us Founded in 2010, eShopWorld powers cross\-border ecommerce for the world’s best\-known brands, creating safer, simpler, and faster shopping experiences for consumers all around the globe. ESW’s powerful combination of technology and human ingenuity optimizes the entire shopper journey, from site development to demand generation to checkout, through shipping, customer service and returns. With configurable end\-to\-end solutions in more than 200 markets worldwide, we fully manage payments, compliance, data security, fraud protection, taxes and tariffs, helping clients enter new markets in as few as 6 weeks, and dramatically improve results in current markets. Bringing together more than 400 experts across multiple disciplines, the ESW team delivers profitable growth for retailers and brands worldwide.




 ]]\>
